# a pair as a value: a word key stays the word as written, any other key is its value (interviewer decision 2026-10-28 for card unknown-name-error; wiki/SPECIFICATION.md `:` pair)
'x = a:1; x is pair'	yes
'a = 5; x = a:1; x'	a:1
'a = 5; x = (a):1; x.key'	5
'x = 1:4; x.value'	4
# a class's instance is no pair, though it holds its fields as one (card class-instance, interviewer OK 2026-11-12); an instance of a subtype of int is a number
'class P { n: int }; P(1) is pair'	no
'class P { n: int }; f(x: any) := x is pair; f(P(1))'	no
'f(x: any) := x is pair; f(a: 1)'	yes
'use color; red is number'	yes
'use color; f(x: any) := x is number; f(red)'	yes
